<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The surface map of the moon's non-spherical gravity potential is first-off much more coarse than that in the notes. The dispersion itself is a little different then the HW4 file due to the altitude of the potential being different but the results above make sense. The map above, evaluated at the surface, would experience more gravitational potential, which is seen in the more intense dispersion. The trend is the intense potentials follow in a line across 40 degrees, which make sense with the moon's oblateness, but I would expect it at 0 degree latittude, so not sure what is going on there.</Text-field>
