<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The resulting orbits make sense that the Earth tracks cyclically with more drifting going on. The simulation differs from the Earth-centered frame and shows a lot more drift. The drift of the moon, which is seen in the higher orbital drift of the Earth in the moon frame, stems from the moon being more influenced by perturbations and the sun. The Earth-moon system is also roughly planar, and that can be seen in the X-position not varying nearly as much as the Y and Z coordinates. </Text-field>
